Script 8: Missing Tool Dependency Guard (check_deps.sh)

Validates that required command-line utilities exist on the system before executing main tasks.

    Concepts: command -v, conditional lists (||), defensive programming.

Bash

#!/bin/bash
set -euo pipefail

REQUIRED_TOOLS=("curl" "jq" "tar" "git")

echo "Verifying environment dependencies..."

for tool in "${REQUIRED_TOOLS[@]}"; do
    if ! command -v "$tool" > /dev/null 2>&1; then
        echo " [ERROR] Required utility '$tool' is not installed."
        MISSING=1
    else
        echo " [OK] Found '$tool' at $(command -v "$tool")"
    fi
done

if [ "${MISSING:-0}" -eq 1 ]; then
    echo "Environment check failed. Install missing dependencies and re-run."
    exit 1
fi

Application: Include at the top of complex installer or setup scripts to fail early with helpful messages if tools are missing.


